{"id":"gem:bialowieza","slug":"poland/bialowieza-forest","schema":"dossier_v2","place":{"name":"Bialowieza Forest","country":"Poland","iso2":"PL","class":"village","lat":52.75,"lon":23.95,"visit_h":2,"categories":["national-park","wilderness","nature","unesco"],"designations":[{"kind":"unesco_whc","name":"UNESCO World Heritage Site"},{"kind":"national_park","name":"UNESCO Man and the Biosphere reserve"}]},"verdict":{"score":7.6,"hidden_gem":false,"confidence":"curated","components":{"beauty":0.4,"appeal":0.779,"depth":0.001,"recognition":1},"country_rank":15,"country_n":81,"country_percentile":82,"class_percentile":83},"sleep":{"beds":{"dorm":25,"private":94,"hotel2":110,"hotel3":160,"hotel4":173,"hotel5":320,"bnb_home":{"2":109,"4":133,"6":177,"8":248},"bnb_room":89},"q":"modelled"},"gallery":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Bialowieza_National_Park_in_Poland0029.JPG/960px-Bialowieza_National_Park_in_Poland0029.JPG","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Bialowieza_National_Park_in_Poland0029.JPG/500px-Bialowieza_National_Park_in_Poland0029.JPG","caption":"Bialowieza Forest","author":"Jacek Karczmarz","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bialowieza_National_Park_in_Poland0029.JPG","w":4288,"h":2848,"ok_print":true}],"intro":{"lead":"Europe's last primeval lowland forest, home to wild bison, giant oaks and UNESCO trails.","body":"The Białowieża Forest and the Białowieża National Park (Polish: Białowieski Park Narodowy) is in Podlaskie Voivodship in Poland and extends across the border into Belarus (this part called Belovezhskaya Pushcha National Park). The Polish part was inscribed into the UNESCO World Heritage List in 1979; the Belarussian part was inscribed in 1992.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Białowieża National Park","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Bia%C5%82owie%C5%BCa_National_Park","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Bialowieza Forest is the last big stretch of old growth woodland in Poland, protected as a national park and listed by UNESCO. The village itself takes 3 hours; the forest takes longer. May to August is the season.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":2670,"visit_h":2}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-bialowieza-national-park","name":"Białowieża National Park","kind":"National park","lat":52.76667,"lon":23.86667,"dist_km":5.9,"rank_score":10.1,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Bialowieza_National_Park_in_Poland0029.JPG/960px-Bialowieza_National_Park_in_Poland0029.JPG","author":"Jacek Karczmarz","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bialowieza_National_Park_in_Poland0029.JPG","w":4288,"h":2848,"ok_print":true}}],"do":[{"name":"European Bison Reservation","type":"activity","detail":"The enclosure where seeing the animals is certain rather than lucky. Around 1,200 of the world's 3,000 wisent live in Poland, all descended from a handful that survived in captivity.","evidence":{"n_sources":9,"of":13,"urls":["https://www.getyourguide.com/warsaw-l41/warsaw-bialowieza-national-park-and-european-bison-tour-t354420/","https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attractions-g274740-Activities-Bialowieza_Podlaskie_Province_Eastern_Poland.html","https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g274740-d4087179-Reviews-European_Bison_Reservation-Bialowieza_Podlaskie_Province_Eastern_Poland.html"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Guided walk in the strict reserve","type":"trail","detail":"The last piece of lowland forest in Europe never cleared or planted, with dead trees left where they fall. Entry only with a licensed guide, and the walk runs about three hours.","evidence":{"n_sources":8,"of":13,"urls":["https://www.backpackadventures.org/bialowieza-forest-poland/","https://wildpoland.com/primeval-bialowieza-forest-biebrza-marshes-wildlife-watching-tour/","https://www.tomdiserens.com/the-strict-reserve/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Wildlife watching at dawn","type":"experience","detail":"Guides take small groups out at first light for the animals that avoid the day: wild bison, elk, wolf tracks and woodpeckers.","evidence":{"n_sources":6,"of":13,"urls":["https://www.backpackadventures.org/bialowieza-forest-poland/","https://wildpoland.com/primeval-bialowieza-forest-biebrza-marshes-wildlife-watching-tour/","https://tourspoland.com/tours-activities/bialowieza-forest-from-warsaw"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Zebra Zubra boardwalk","type":"trail","detail":"A raised plank trail over the swampy part of the forest, running out to the bison reserve. Free and open to anyone.","evidence":{"n_sources":5,"of":13,"urls":["https://www.thebudgetsavvytravelers.com/bialoweiza-forest/","https://www.backpackadventures.org/bialowieza-forest-poland/","https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attractions-g274740-Activities-Bialowieza_Podlaskie_Province_Eastern_Poland.html"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Narrow gauge forest railway","type":"activity","detail":"Built in the First World War to haul timber and run until the 1990s. Trains still work the Hajnowka to Topilo stretch in season, straight through the forest.","season":[5,6,7,8,9],"evidence":{"n_sources":4,"of":13,"urls":["https://bartekonthego.com/bialowieza-forest-national-park-poland-places-to-see-things-to-do-guide/","https://bialowieza.travel/en/you-must-see/bialowieza-national-park","https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Bia%C5%82owie%C5%BCa_National_Park"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"The village's wooden architecture","type":"activity","detail":"Carved timber houses along the road, and a tsarist railway station restored at the end of it, from when this was a hunting estate of the Russian court.","evidence":{"n_sources":4,"of":13,"urls":["https://en.wikivoyage.org/